    Selectable->False],
   DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
   ImageSizeRaw->{1536., 1024.},
   PlotRange->{{0, 1536.}, {0, 1024.}}],
  StripOnInput->False,
  Magnification->0.55 Inherited]], "Output",
 CellFrame->False,ExpressionUUID->"05cc6976-a402-467c-84d6-d9d4d2604a6a"],

Cell["\<\
Two windows on two algebras. Left: the smooth, continuous world of classical \
arithmetic (R, +, *). Right: the same landscape under (max, +) -- every \
operation produces a crisp polyhedral surface. The two are connected by a \
small bridge.\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Helvetica",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"75b2b8b3-d4cb-425f-bf2e-3d1c876c085e"],

Cell["1.  The max-plus semiring in 60 seconds", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ed74adcd-27b5-4741-a2dc-42a9083942da"],

Cell["\<\
The tropical (max-plus) semiring is the set of real numbers extended with \
negative infinity,\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2045e38a-45ef-4950-ab0d-0531cb46d96d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SubscriptBox["R", "max"], "=", 
  RowBox[{"R", "\[Union]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}], "}"}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"2610a865-48b9-406b-a301-a09d07587eb5"],

Cell["\<\
equipped with two operations that look like the addition and multiplication \
of classical algebra but are:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"18260c2c-ecca-4e19-9a8e-9db75be89ee2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", "\[CirclePlus]", "b"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{"max", "(", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", "b"}], ")"}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"94e2d14c-5948-4292-9f9b-e1b00c549a2d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", "\[CircleTimes]", "b"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{"a", "+", "b"}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"a3ba8e21-42e0-442c-ba11-d5dfaf35e161"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The identities flip: the additive identity is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b3c6896b-68a4-4c4c-8fa3-2a508ef2ea94"],
 " (since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"max", "(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}], ",", "a"}], ")"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0a8613e1-857a-4e14-941c-cfb06f643c71"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["a",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "552b5987-fb49-4cc9-9577-f005e3c252a5"],
 "), and the multiplicative identity is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["0",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5ec2b417-cf4d-47e4-8be7-4509242c6f38"],
 " (since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"0", "+", "a"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "95f7e683-4c81-46f5-a4f7-ffd38f79f29c"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["a",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a8a2aa6e-a186-49aa-a793-eda9388b6017"],
 "). Apart from the absence of additive inverses (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     SubscriptBox["R", "\"\<max\>\""],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "37c54da5-ca7b-45bf-983a-70dc09326ca3"],
 " is a semiring, not a ring), every familiar axiom of a commutative ring \
carries over. Distributivity in particular: "
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13286cd3-b3ef-46b6-a1a1-0c8080b6f484"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", "\[CircleTimes]", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"b", "\[CirclePlus]", "c"}], ")"}]}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", "\[CircleTimes]", "b"}], "\[CirclePlus]", 
      RowBox[{"a", "\[CircleTimes]", "c"}]}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"50ca78d0-1fca-4617-aba1-f8d23aede86d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is worth pausing on what this re-labelling really buys you. Classical \
addition and multiplication are continuous and smooth, whereas ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["Max",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "53b8142e-544f-4ac5-8ca7-58d8c1e36a47"],
 " has a non-differentiable corner. So every identity of ordinary algebra \
translates into an identity about piecewise-linear convex functions. \
Polynomials become piecewise-linear functions. Powers become repeated \
max-with-translation. The distributive law becomes the statement that ",
 StyleBox["a classical sum of convex piecewise-linear functions is again a \
convex piecewise-linear function",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " -- a deeply non-obvious fact in ordinary analysis, but a trivial \
consequence of the semiring axioms once you have the right operator names. \
This is the lever the rest of the post pulls on."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"24d42964-8385-428c-b552-868af6b20ea0"],

Cell["Operators in WL", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"87dce79d-cce1-41de-9486-b3dcf2574fe0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We attach the definitions of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["CirclePlus",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "14a6039c-14c8-4504-a9c6-0d4248ee165a"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["CircleTimes",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8bb0b570-d707-4ca6-ab93-f538a5a983df"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["CircleDot",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0375030c-e76a-466a-8137-f0816f2a78a7"],
 " to the System` symbols once, so the standard infix syntax just works. The \
Listable, Flat, OneIdentity, Orderless attributes give us elementwise \
behaviour, n-ary forms, and the simplifications a commutative associative \
operator should have."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b01dbd8d-8fb2-49b1-898d-4001cd54f050"],

Cell["\<\
Unprotect[System`CirclePlus, System`CircleTimes, System`CircleDot];

System`CirclePlus[a_, b_]   := Max[a, b];
System`CirclePlus[a_, b__]  := Max[a, b];
SetAttributes[System`CirclePlus, {Listable, Flat, OneIdentity, Orderless}];

System`CircleTimes[a_, b_]  := a + b;
System`CircleTimes[a_, b__] := Plus[a, b];
SetAttributes[System`CircleTimes, {Listable, Flat, OneIdentity, Orderless}];

System`CircleDot[A_?MatrixQ, B_?MatrixQ] := Inner[Plus, A, B, Max];
System`CircleDot[A_?MatrixQ, v_?VectorQ] := Inner[Plus, A, v, Max];
System`CircleDot[v_?VectorQ, A_?MatrixQ] := Inner[Plus, v, A, Max];

Protect[System`CirclePlus, System`CircleTimes, System`CircleDot];

{3 \\[CirclePlus] 7,  3 \\[CircleTimes] 7,
 {1, 2, 3} \\[CirclePlus] {4, 0, 5},
 {1, 2, 3} \\[CircleTimes] 10}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a1df4b44-5958-4813-86c1-4619d753e450"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"7", ",", "10", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"4", ",", "2", ",", "5"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"11", ",", "12", ",", "13"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",Expression\
UUID->"e234d39f-07c2-4943-aad4-ca0668400ff3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The list arithmetic comes for free because of the Listable attribute. The \
first two scalar results say that, in max-plus, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"3", "\[CirclePlus]", "7"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "08b7f3e8-eb5c-42cf-b12e-f9e9ce9d289e"],
 " is 7 (the larger of the two) and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"3", "\[CircleTimes]", "7"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ef5cac79-2fde-4d65-8c79-8922e14c254b"],
 " is 10 (their classical sum). The vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}], "}"}], "\[CirclePlus]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"4", ",", "0", ",", "5"}], "}"}]}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "496ab78f-b85b-42e0-a353-14266e30be2f"],
 " is the elementwise max ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"4", ",", "2", ",", "5"}], "}"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "abdeb171-4f0e-4bed-b5e2-fd6d2dd1668b"],
 ". The last expression scales every entry by 10 in the tropical sense, which \
is classical addition of 10 to each."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bb2c8c45-7e93-40bf-acf6-2cfdef09f5cb"],

Cell["2.  Tropical vectors and matrices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c6ce1e32-f1a9-4434-89d9-fd25da496b60"],

Cell["\<\
A tropical vector or matrix is just a real array; what changes is the \
multiplication. The tropical matrix product replaces the usual \"sum of \
products\" with \"max of sums\":\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4eb9ff95-659d-4867-99ec-a0d6ea9c9b0b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"A", "\[CircleDot]", "B"}], 
      RowBox[{"i", ",", "j"}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["Max", "k"], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["A", 
         RowBox[{"i", ",", "k"}]], "+", 
        SubscriptBox["B", 
         RowBox[{"k", ",", "j"}]]}], ")"}]}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"607a38ed-8c65-4bdd-ba64-9dd428628deb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "implemented as ",
 StyleBox["Inner[Plus, A, B, Max]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 " in WL. The identity matrix has 0 on the diagonal and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "deee8ad9-079f-41cd-a0e3-8677e1da170a"],
 " elsewhere (since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "67e8599a-527b-42cf-bee7-9e67018894ec"],
 " is the new \"zero\")."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ec2a721a-56aa-4ac0-9252-788aeb3365bf"],

Cell["\<\
MPIdentity[n_Integer] :=
  Normal @ SparseArray[{i_, i_} -> 0, {n, n}, -Infinity];

MPMatrixPower[A_, 0]  := MPIdentity[Length[A]];
MPMatrixPower[A_, 1]  := A;
MPMatrixPower[A_, k_] := Nest[A \\[CircleDot] # &, A, k - 1];

A = {{1, 2}, {3, 0}};
B = {{0, -1}, {2, 4}};
{
  \"A . B (classical)\"     -> A . B,
  \"A \\[CircleDot] B\"     -> A \\[CircleDot] B,
  \"A^2 (classical)\"       -> MatrixPower[A, 2],
  \"A^2 (tropical)\"        -> MPMatrixPower[A, 2],
  \"MPIdentity[2] \\[CircleDot] A\" ->
                                MPIdentity[2] \\[CircleDot] A
} // TableForm\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e980cec1-1b65-4705-8417-430cc011dba3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  TagBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{"\<\"A . B (classical)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"4", ",", "7"}], "}"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", 
           RowBox[{"-", "3"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]},
     {
      RowBox[{"\<\"A \[CircleDot] B\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"4", ",", "6"}], "}"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"3", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]},
     {
      RowBox[{"\<\"A^2 (classical)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"7", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"3", ",", "6"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]},
     {
      RowBox[{"\<\"A^2 (tropical)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"5", ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"4", ",", "5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]},
     {
      RowBox[{"\<\"MPIdentity[2] \[CircleDot] A\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"3", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[0.5599999999999999]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}],
   Column],
  Function[BoxForm`e$, 
   TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output",
 CellFrame->False,ExpressionUUID->"4f1a93d5-1139-45c5-9e66-6b1ff912d4e3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compare the second row: classical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"A", ".", "B"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2b0e22c8-5f0a-4e0f-91d6-4721fa01b8d1"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
        {"4", "6"},
        {"6", 
         RowBox[{"-", "3"}]}
       },
       GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
       GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
           Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
            Offset[0.7]}, 
           Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
           Offset[0.2], {
            Offset[0.4]}, 
           Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "231ee71e-a503-4941-b833-7d65a285208d"],
 " whereas tropical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"A", "\[CircleDot]", "B"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1c030e4a-d403-450c-bde3-3a12e0dedfa6"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
        {"4", "6"},
        {"3", "4"}
       },
       GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
       GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
           Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
            Offset[0.7]}, 
           Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
           Offset[0.2], {
            Offset[0.4]}, 
           Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "781a3267-bd9d-4fd9-9043-7d1d24654fc7"],
 ". Entry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     SubscriptBox["\"\<(A\[CircleDot]B)\>\"", "\"\<1,1\>\""],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "bd33b542-f91a-4bf3-81a6-061361dcc141"],
 " of the tropical product is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"max", "(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"1", "+", "0"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"2", "+", "2"}]}], ")"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fa1c04fa-7453-4b75-9f11-6f20050bb6e9"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["4",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3429b1be-0b41-44cb-884f-81c5b549f7ad"],
 ", and so on. The identity matrix really is an identity: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[ImaginaryI]", "2"], "\[CircleDot]", "A"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1067b004-e883-4657-ae48-ceca51ca3680"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["A",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "84c7fba3-d6a0-4f96-b202-6f1c1bae6c5b"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"71d0e690-a640-49cb-bfb1-a1d9ac80ee9c"],

Cell["The Kleene star", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"e2a6ff03-790d-4614-bc25-571fc1f196f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a square tropical matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["A",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "94d3404a-d829-46df-9208-76abb344e2ac"],
 " the Kleene star (\"transitive closure\" in min-plus) is"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"61198844-c26d-4c36-896f-6d23b8466705"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"A", "\"*\""},
      "Superscript"], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[ImaginaryI]", "n"], "\[CirclePlus]", "A", "\[CirclePlus]", 
      TemplateBox[{"A", 
        RowBox[{"\[CircleTimes]", "2"}]},
       "Superscript"], "\[CirclePlus]", 
      TemplateBox[{"A", 
        RowBox[{"\[CircleTimes]", "3"}]},
       "Superscript"], "\[CirclePlus]", "\[Ellipsis]"}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"eac4a5d1-9cf0-4ec9-ae24-51da98b433e2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "i.e. the matrix whose ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     SubscriptBox["\"\<A^*\>\"", "\"\<i,j\>\""],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8b45f361-798a-46e4-8f10-da516bbab488"],
 " entry is the largest-weight path of any length from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["i",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "563fc6fa-ffec-472a-9513-21149c7aa5e5"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["j",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3f4541d3-3782-4baf-941a-2db167462e4f"],
 ". On a graph with no positive-weight cycle the series stabilises after at \
most ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f8fe4189-b033-45a7-8b0f-15ef9b1ecc3a"],
 " products. We compute it explicitly:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eeffc03f-ba84-489e-86d2-2a2e1cdc774a"],

Cell["\<\
KleeneStar[A_?MatrixQ] := Module[{n = Length[A], acc, term},
  acc  = MPIdentity[n];
  term = MPIdentity[n];
  Do[
    term = A \\[CircleDot] term;
    acc  = MapThread[Max, {acc, term}, 2],
    {n - 1}];
  acc
];

(* longest-path matrix of a DAG with three nodes and two edges *)
adj = {{-Infinity, 2, -Infinity},
       {-Infinity, -Infinity, 3},
       {-Infinity, -Infinity, -Infinity}};
KleeneStar[adj] // MatrixForm\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8f8b88d1-6a43-4ff4-b070-e277e22fc524"],

