 ". WL's Simplify says yes:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"daf9017c-0281-4358-a566-9fe5faf1f759"],

Cell["\<\
ClearAll[a, b, c, w, e, x1, x2];
hExpr  = Max[0, a x1 + b x2 + c];
fOrig  = w hExpr + e;
fAlt   = Piecewise[{{Max[e, w (a x1 + b x2 + c) + e], w > 0},
                    {e - Max[0, -w (a x1 + b x2 + c)],  w < 0},
                    {e,                                 w == 0}}];

(* test numerically over a random parameter sweep *)
SeedRandom[42];
Module[{vals},
  vals = Table[
    Module[{r = RandomReal[{-2, 2}, 7]},
      With[{aa = r[[1]], bb = r[[2]], cc = r[[3]], ww = r[[4]],
            ee = r[[5]], xa = r[[6]], xb = r[[7]]},
        Abs[fOrig - fAlt /. {a -> aa, b -> bb, c -> cc, w -> ww,
                              e -> ee, x1 -> xa, x2 -> xb}]
      ]],
    {500}];
  Max[vals]
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"35f54dd4-f222-4644-865c-1b12d3d3b2fc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "(Evaluating this cell prints ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["0.`",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1ae86d2b-0954-4ce7-8a39-dc0dbb725527"],
 ".  The two expressions are identical on every numerical sample.)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"92bf9f9f-41a2-44ee-a15f-e33e16322c21"],

Cell["11.  Symbolic derivation: 2 \[Rule] 2 \[Rule] 1 network", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6fd69294-be48-40bf-a388-578b1b136769"],

Cell["\<\
With two hidden units we can already produce a non-trivial tropical rational \
(mixed signs) or a tropical polynomial with four monomials (both signs \
positive). Let\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"85675cd4-5b7f-4027-a23c-769f1b5db268"],

